MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4b3f2a8c8f344355b16a4d4296ae3f98, type: 3}
  m_Name: BrittleStar
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  vesselClass: 16
  entries:
  - Element: 1
    AbilityLabel: Charge Mode
    AbilityDescription: 'RB. FIVE CORDS, one from each turret, slicing every prism they touch (any domain; your own fresh
      trail is spared) and striking rival hulls for petals. Released, RT leaves them WHIPS at 150%
      length: heavy, inextensible, slow - a turn, a ring flick or a sweep of the right stick sends a
      wave travelling down them that rings on for seconds. Pulled, RT shortens them to 100% and
      stiffens them into five SABERS that keep 60% of the whip''s give (analog: every depth in
      between). The right stick turns them with the ring and opens them out. Using them cools the
      guns. LT throws the ring - only with a SPARE ring in stock (one per crystal, two at most); the
      mounted ring then regrows on its own. It blows on contact or its fuse in a disk as wide as the
      cell''s nucleus, bursting out of the ring as faceted volumes - five coiling arms led by
      crystals, five crests and the ring''s own pentagon - still spinning, destroying every prism in
      its plane and stripping petals from every rival hull it crosses (petals only - nothing is
      moved). The card shows the spare stock. Charge is threat - one dial: the cords'' cut width and
      the rounds'' size x1 -> x1.8 at level 10 (projectileScaleMultiplier), the disk''s thickness x1
      -> x4 on top of its x4 base, 4 to 16 times the ring''s (blastScale).'
    Input: 3
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: 
    UpgradeDescription: 
  - Element: 2
    AbilityLabel: Creation Mode
    AbilityDescription: 'B. A trail behind EACH of the ring''s five corners instead of the single small block from the
      cockpit - the same small block, five lines that turn with the ring''s firing rotation. The
      SLOWEST mode: cruise x0.5. Mass is girth - one dial: the width and height of EVERY block you
      lay, the base trail''s and the corner trails'', x1 -> x2 at level 10, never their length
      (BrittleStarConfigSO.prismWidthScale).'
    Input: 7
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: 
    UpgradeDescription: 
  - Element: 3
    AbilityLabel: Space Mode
    AbilityDescription: 'X. FIVE GUNS: RT fires every turret, its pull setting the rate (analog, up to 90 rounds/s each;
      the Sparrow''s round at 135 u/s, swelling as it flies, 387 u reach). The right stick''s
      direction turns the ring, and the guns with it; its deflection moves them in and out: centred
      they meet 120 u ahead (the vessel a crosshair), pushed to the rim they splay 25 degrees. In
      every other mode RT fires the one turret the ring has turned to the aim, the same gun with no
      spread. Every round HEATS the guns - heat per second is the pull x the guns firing - and
      overheated they cannot fire until they cool; overheated in Space Mode your trail lays DANGER
      prisms. The card shows the heat. Friendly fire is on. A round on a rival hull is a scored bullet
      hit (petals only). Space is reach and endurance: every gun''s range x1 -> x2 at level 10
      (BrittleStarConfigSO.rangeMultiplier), and the heat the guns hold x1 -> x3.33, so a full
      five-gun burst runs ~6 s at level 0 and ~20 s at level 10 (BrittleStarConfigSO.heatCapacity).'
    Input: 8
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: 
    UpgradeDescription: 
  - Element: 4
    AbilityLabel: Speed Mode
    AbilityDescription: 'A. Ignite every thruster: the hull''s cruise speed x6, the base trail''s spacing stretched by
      the same ratio so production per second does not rise, and every prism stretched with it so the
      trail still joins up. Time is rate - one dial: Speed Mode''s multiplier x6 -> x8 at level 10
      (BrittleStarConfigSO.speedModeMultiplier).'
    Input: 6
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: 
    UpgradeDescription: 
